+    // WHY, AND IT IS THE CAMERA, NOT THE UI. The queue is drained once per frame and every
+    // queued move is delivered, so a frame that saw N moves calls CPythonApplication::
+    // OnMouseMove N times. That is harmless for the UI — the last position wins — but it is
+    // NOT harmless for the camera drag, because BgfxCamera::Drag RE-ANCHORS on every call
+    // (BgfxCamera.cpp:1221-1222). Each call therefore measures only the movement since the
+    // PREVIOUS event, and each one OVERWRITES angularVelocity rather than adding to it
