+    // inter-event delta alone and the other N-1 deltas are thrown away, so the camera turns
+    // roughly 1/N of the distance the mouse actually travelled.
+    //
+    // N is "browser mousemove rate divided by frame rate", so the SLOWER the renderer the
+    // WORSE it gets — which is why this reads as "the camera rotation is far too slow" on a
+    // software-rendered build and not on a fast one. It is a frame-rate coupling introduced
+    // by the queue, not by the sensitivity: m_fResistance is 0.3 here exactly as in the
+    // original (Camera.cpp:9).
