+    // desktop delta already covers the whole frame. Win32 coalesces WM_MOUSEMOVE in the
+    // message queue for the same reason. Delivering the final position once per frame is
+    // what both of them already do.
+    //
+    // ONLY AN ADJACENT RUN IS COLLAPSED, which is what keeps ordering intact: a move that
+    // precedes a button press is still queued before it, because the press breaks the run
