+		// of those for every labelled button: a TextLine parented to the button, placed at
+		// the button's CENTRE, never sized. On that one pixel the loop above descended
+		// into the label and returned it, so the button got neither OnMouseOverIn nor
+		// OnMouseLeftButtonUp -- a dead pixel in the middle of every button, which is
+		// precisely where anything aiming at "the button" aims.
+		//
+		// Only for windows that HAVE a parent. __PickWindow compares a layer's result
+		// against the layer BY IDENTITY to decide whether anything was hit, so a layer
+		// must go on returning itself even when it carries no size of its own.
+		//
+		// FLAG_IGNORE_SIZE means "my rect does not describe me"; those keep their answer.
+		if (m_pParent && 0 == m_lWidth && 0 == m_lHeight &&
+		    !IsFlag(CWindow::FLAG_IGNORE_SIZE))
+			return nullptr;
+
 		return (this);
 	}
 
